 "title": "Do You Know a Hijacked Bus Sent 125,000 People to the Real Vice City? #shorts",
 "intro": {
  "mood": "tension",
  "beats": [
   {
    "say": "Do you know a hijacked bus in Havana sent a hundred and twenty five thousand people to the real Vice City?",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "day",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "town",
       "y": 0.75,
       "n": 12,
       "gap": 140,
       "h": 160,
       "col": "#d8c8a8",
       "night": false,
       "depth": 0.4
      },
      {
       "type": "bus",
       "x": 0.5,
       "y": 0.92,
       "s": 0.8,
       "depth": 0.7,
       "drive": [
        1.3,
        0.45,
        0,
        3
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "do": [],
    "cam": {
     "lon": -82.37,
     "lat": 23.11,
     "scale": 9000
    }
   },
   {
    "say": "The first of April 1980. Héctor Sanyustiz and four friends empty a city bus, route 79, by pretending it has broken down.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "day",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "town",
       "y": 0.75,
       "n": 10,
       "gap": 140,
       "h": 160,
       "col": "#d8c8a8",
       "night": false,
       "depth": 0.4
      },
      {
       "type": "bus",
       "x": 0.5,
       "y": 0.95,
       "s": 0.9,
       "depth": 0.7
      },
      {
       "type": "crowd",
       "y": 1.0,
       "n": 16,
       "hats": false,
       "depth": 0.8
      }
     ]
    },
    "do": []
   },
   {
    "talk": [
     {
      "who": "DRV",
      "text": "Everybody off. The bus is broken."
     },
     {
      "who": "HEC",
      "text": "Stay on the bus."
     }
    ],
    "bg": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "day",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "bus",
       "x": 0.5,
       "y": 1.02,
       "s": 1.3,
       "depth": 0.7
      }
     ],
     "push": 0.1
    }
   },
   {
    "say": "Then he floors it, through the fence of the Peruvian embassy. Guards open fire. One guard is killed in the crossfire.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "day",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "fence",
       "y": 0.86,
       "h": 220,
       "depth": 0.6,
       "broken": 0.55
      },
      {
       "type": "bus",
       "x": 0.55,
       "y": 0.95,
       "s": 0.8,
       "depth": 0.7
      }
     ],
     "fx": [
      "dust",
      "smoke"
     ],
     "push": 0.15
    },
    "do": []
   },
   {
    "say": "Peru refuses to hand them back. So Castro pulls every guard away from the embassy. In about two days, ten thousand eight hundred people pour in.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "day",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "fence",
       "y": 0.86,
       "h": 220,
       "depth": 0.6
      },
      {
       "type": "crowd",
       "y": 1.0,
       "n": 140,
       "hats": false,
       "depth": 0.8
      }
     ],
     "push": 0.05
    },
    "do": []
   },
   {
    "say": "Then he opens the port of Mariel to anyone who wants to leave. Exiles in Miami sail south to fetch their families.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "day",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "sea",
       "y": 0.56,
       "depth": 0.3
      },
      {
       "type": "boats",
       "n": 4,
       "y": 0.72,
       "x": 0.12,
       "gap": 0.22,
       "s": 0.7,
       "drift": 1,
       "crowded": true,
       "depth": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    "do": []
   },
   {
    "say": "By October, about a hundred and twenty five thousand Cubans have crossed to Florida. Most of them settle in Miami. All because of one bus.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "night",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "city",
       "y": 0.72,
       "night": true,
       "neon": true,
